\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Critic value $V(s)$ vs.\ episodic return $G_t$ for collapsed (008d, left) and healthy (008a, right) configurations. The collapsed critic's predictions are \emph  {negatively} correlated with actual returns ($r = {-}0.20$), indicating delusional value ranking: states assigned higher value actually produce \emph  {lower} returns. The healthy critic maintains positive correlation ($r = {+}0.54$) despite comparable overestimation rates (92.7\% vs.\ 82.8\%), demonstrating that bias magnitude is not the distinguishing pathology; value-return \emph  {ordering} is.}}{23}{figure.caption.72}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:value_vs_returns}{{11}{23}{Critic value $V(s)$ vs.\ episodic return $G_t$ for collapsed (008d, left) and healthy (008a, right) configurations. The collapsed critic's predictions are \emph {negatively} correlated with actual returns ($r = {-}0.20$), indicating delusional value ranking: states assigned higher value actually produce \emph {lower} returns. The healthy critic maintains positive correlation ($r = {+}0.54$) despite comparable overestimation rates (92.7\% vs.\ 82.8\%), demonstrating that bias magnitude is not the distinguishing pathology; value-return \emph {ordering} is}{figure.caption.72}{}}
